 "title": "Placements | IIM Bangalore",
 "text": "General Information\n\nThe placement process for the programme is thoughtfully designed to connect students with recruiters from diverse industries, both national and global.\n\nPlacements begin with Pre-Placement Talks (PPTs) by recruiters, where they share insights into their organizations, roles, and expectations. Students then express their interest by submitting detailed resumes through the Career Development Services (CDS) portal.\n\nRecruiters review applications, create a shortlist, and coordinate with the student driven Placement team to schedule interviews. The process includes both on-campus and off-campus interviews to ensure a comprehensive match between candidates and organizations. The process typically commences in November and spans several months, allowing flexibility for both recruiters and students.\n\nTo ensure student success, the Career Development Services team provides extensive support through resume workshops, personality tests, interview skill enhancement sessions, and career counseling.\n\nPlacement Highlights\nMean Median Salary over the​years (In Lakhs)\n36.5​36.5\n33.1​33.1\n34.33​34.33\n33.07​33.07\n31.63​31.63\n37.1​37.1\n35.5​35.5\n33​33\n32.21​32.21\n30​30\nMean Salary\nMedian Salary\n0\n10\n20\n30\n40\n2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n\n Mean Salary\n\n Median Salary\n\nNo. of students in placement process ​& No. of students with offers\n66​66\n72​72\n72​72\n70​70\n72​72\n66​66\n72​72\n70​70\n70​70\n72​72\nstudents in placement process\nstudents with successful offers\n0\n20\n40\n60\n80\n2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n\n Students in process\n\n Students with offers\n\nTotal percent market share\nNo. Of companies who made offers over the​years\n25​25\n31​31\n29​29\n27​27\n26​26\n2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n0\n10\n20\n30\n40\n\n \n\nPast Recruiters\nPast Roles\nArea Sales Manager\tHead of Technology\nAssistant Director\tHead of Marketing\nAssistant General Manager\tImplementation Coach\nAssistant Vice President\tImplementation Consultant\nAssociate Manager\tManager\nAssociate Manager (AI Product and Advisory)\tManager (Data & AI)\nAssociate Vice President\tManager of Excellence\nAsst. Engagement Manager\tManager Strategic Initiatives\nAVP, F&A Operations\tOperations Manager\nAVP, Operations\tPre-Sales\nAVP, Tech Services\tProduct Manager\nAVP, Global Markets Front Office\tProduct Owner (IT)\nBI Consultant \tProgram Manager\nBusiness Development Manager\tProject Manager\nChief Manager\tSenior Business Manager\nCluster Manager\tSenior Consultant\nCompetency Leader\tSenior Digital Product Manager\nConsultant (Data & AI)\tSenior Financial Analyst \nCustomer Relationship Manager\tSenior Manager\nDirector \tSenior Manager, Strategy \nDirector, Operations\tSenior Program Manager\nEngagement Manager\tSpecialist Process Design\nGeneral Manager\tStrategic Trends Lead\nGroup Finance Manager\tVice President\nRecruiter Testimonials\n\n S&C has been hiring from the EPGP programme in IIMB for over 10 years now. The first person we hired from the EPGP batch (2013-2014) is still part of our team and doing extremely well. We have observed a consistent quality in the candidates who come from this college, each one bringing in a unique blend of skills and industry experience. Every year, we look forward to meeting the new batch and exploring how we can work together to achieve success.\n\n \n\nGanesan Ramachandran, Managing Director – Tech Strategy and Advisory\n\nAccenture\n\n Recruiting top talent from IIMB EPGP batch for the last few years, and my association began last year. I have been involved in a variety of activities, including the selection process, knowledge sharing, and leadership interactions with students who come from diverse industry backgrounds and possess rich experience. I am truly impressed by the quality and depth of the curriculum, which effectively caters to industry needs. The high-calibre talent we have onboarded over the years has played a crucial role in our organisation. We look forward to continued engagement with IIMB in the coming years.\n\nArijit Maitra, SVP, Enterprise Applications\n\nSutherland\n\n The quality of students is top class and the professionals we have hired are proving to be assets to our organisation. Thank you to the team for helping us conduct a smooth placement process.\n\nTalent Acquisition Team\n\nInfosys\n\n The EPGP at IIMB is designed to meet the expectations of experienced professionals taking up challenging roles in the industry. Students recruited from the programme have augured well in different roles, ranging from value stream consulting to technology consulting engagements, and continue to raise the bar within our organisation. The programme also enables us to pick professionals from varied domains and backgrounds enabling us to build a diverse set of future leaders.\n\nTalent Acquisition Team, Premier Campus Recruitment Team\n\n Larsen & Toubro\n\nPlacement Brochure\n2027\n2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n2021\nPlacement Statistics\nContact\n\nAssociate Manager - CDS\n\nReena Fernandes\n\n +91-80-26993655\n reenaf[at]iimb[dot]ac[dot]in\n\nCDS Office:\n\n +91-80-26993301\ncds[at]iimb[dot]ac[dot]in\n\nEPGP Placement Committee:\n\n epgpplace[at]iimb[dot]ac[dot]in\n\n \n\n ",
